package local:uni;

// The import surface for the compact --no-gc --component output WHEN THE PROGRAM PRINTS
// (the print micro-adapter). A print-free --no-gc component imports NOTHING (the
// adapter-free reactor wrap); a printing one needs exactly wasi:cli/stdout@0.3.0 (which
// pulls wasi:cli/types@0.3.0 in for the error-code enum) so a tiny bridge core module can
// implement the core's single wasi_snapshot_preview1.fd_write import over
// write-via-stream + the async stream/future built-ins, parking on a blocking
// waitable-set.wait when one reports BLOCKED -- all of base component-model-async
// (default-on in wasmtime 46+), so the component still runs with ZERO flags; the exports
// become async lifts because only an async-typed task may block.
//
// fd 1 only: --no-gc rejects every other I/O op at compile time (print/princ/terpri are
// the whole printing surface), so wasi:cli/stderr would be dead weight in the block.
//
// The interface order fixes the component import-instance indices
// NoGcWasmComponentBuilder assumes (wasi:cli/types is dependency-hoisted first); append
// new interfaces LAST and re-derive the constants from a fresh `wasm-tools dump`.
world uni-nogc-print {
  import wasi:cli/stdout@0.3.0;
}
